  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Population Fund (UNFPA) core funding 2022-2023 to-2026-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Population Fund (UNFPA) is a key organisation supporting progress towards global achievement of the health and gender equality targets of the Sustainable Development Goals. It calls for the realisation of sexual and reproductive health and rights for all. It works with governments and non-government partners to promote universal access to quality, comprehensive and  integrated sexual and reproductive health services. This includes, for example, rights based family planning, comprehensive sexuality education and youth leadership. It aims to empower people, particularly young people, to exercise autonomy, choice and participation with regard to their sexual and reproductive health and rights. Australia provides UNFPA with annual core voluntary contributions (AUD9.5 million annually) to support the implementation of its Strategic Plan 2022-25 and approved successor plans.</narrative>
  </description>
